  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Ngữ pháp · đã + verbo (el pasado)",
    "@en": "Ngữ pháp · đã + verb (past)"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**đã** delante del verbo puede señalar que una acción ya ocurrió: **Tôi đã đi làm** = ya fui / he ido a trabajar.",
     "@en": "**đã** in front of the verb may point out that an action has already happened: **Tôi đã đi làm** = I have already been / have gone to work."
    },
    {
     "@es": "Si el contexto ya deja claro cuándo ocurrió, a menudo se omite: **Hôm qua tôi đi làm** = ayer fui a trabajar. No es una conjugación obligatoria del pasado.",
     "@en": "If the context already makes it clear when it happened, it is often omitted: **Hôm qua tôi đi làm** = yesterday I went to work. It's not a mandatory conjugation from the past."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "dialogo",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Ejemplos: đã",
    "@en": "Examples: đã"
   },
   "frases": [
